# .env.example - copy to .env, and set what this machine has. .env is not committed.
#
# The scripts in docker/ read .env (docker/host.sh). A line is NAME=value, and the value is the rest of the line as it
# is: a path with spaces needs no quotes. A variable that the environment sets keeps its value.

# Where the games are installed, for the dev server and the game tests. Name the folders of the games this machine has,
# at least one, and remove the other lines. The folders are only read. These are where Steam installs the games on
# Windows. Black Ops III takes two folders: the game, and Steam's tool Call of Duty: Black Ops III - Unranked Dedicated
# Server, which is in Steam's library under Tools.
ZOMBIES_T5=C:/Program Files (x86)/Steam/steamapps/common/Call of Duty Black Ops
ZOMBIES_T6=C:/Program Files (x86)/Steam/steamapps/common/Call of Duty Black Ops II
ZOMBIES_T7=C:/Program Files (x86)/Steam/steamapps/common/Call of Duty Black Ops III
ZOMBIES_T7_SERVER=C:/Program Files (x86)/Steam/steamapps/common/Call of Duty Black Ops III 545990
